uya; Alexandre Gramfort; Rémi Gribonval; Matthieu\nHeitz; Maarten V. de Hoop; Geert-Jan Huizing; Samuel Hurault; Hicham Janati;\nJérémie Kalfon; Cyril Letrouit; Flavien Leger; Sibylle Marcotte; Arthur Mensch;\nThomas Moreau; Boris Muzellec; Luca Nenna; Clarice Poon; Julien Rabin; Zakaria\nRamzi; Pierre Roussillon; Jules Samaran; Michael Sander; Meyer Scetbon; Othmane\nSebbouh; Justin Solomon; Thibault Séjourné; François-Xavier Vialard; Zhenzhang\nYe; and Kelvin S. Zhang. Their ideas, taste, questions and generosity have\nshaped the mathematical atmosphere in which this book was written.","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"hChenIAOCy"}],"key":"ZBVY9KOkhe"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finally, my deepest and most personal thanks go to my three children, Mael,\nCamille and Arthur, and to my love, Gwenn Guichaoua. I am lucky to share with\nher a passion for mathematics, computer science and biology.","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"oMN4moBeJ6"}],"key":"IV5X1mtGB3"}],"key":"tciZpLpLCn"}],"key":"fAWtIZjmNl"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Optimal Transport for Machine Learners","url":"/","group":"Optimal Transport for Machine Learners"},"next":{"title":"Optimal Matching between Point Clouds","url":"/matching","group":"Chapters"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}